sen0414:Deck_Ch04_3e a schema:LearningResource ; dcterms:title "Chapter 4: Functions - renewed for the 3rd edition" ;
    dcterms:format "application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.presentationml.presentation" ;
    cme:fileInPart "03-materials/ch04/SEN0414_Ch04_Functions_3e_v1_1_0.pptx" ;
    cme:renewalStatus "Redesigned for the classroom on 2026-10-06 to the CME materials look-and-feel standard v1.0.0 (shared renderer, the >>> chip): 25 numbered warm-ivory slides, agenda with exact ranges, summary before the live-linked resources, takeaway strips throughout. Program-first: 17 whole programs with their transcripts carry the chapter - the mutable-default trap and repair, the call stack inspected from inside, the UnboundLocalError on its own slide, global/nonlocal, try placement inside-vs-outside, Collatz fed real input, input validation, deferred annotations - each panel captioned name-and-lines and verified by program_check_v2_0_1.py (verbatim slices; transcripts re-executed with recorded inputs, input echoes handled), with deck_check re-running the console rows, 0 mismatches. VERSION TRUTH both ways: the chapter demonstrates PEP 758 (except without parentheses), so the whole recording was re-executed under an installed Python 3.14.6 and the checks ran under that interpreter - the same file is a SyntaxError under 3.13, and the slide says exactly that. Three dated, sourced 5N1K stories with fact rows and live links: David Wheeler's 1952 closed subroutine on EDSAC (the Cambridge Computer Laboratory photograph, CC BY 2.0, credit on-slide), the Collatz conjecture presented honestly as open since 1937, and PEP 758 demonstrated rather than quoted. Width and height gates keep code from wrapping (a pre-build audit sizes every panel from the recording); the layout check found no overflowing frame. Licences in 03-materials/ch04/assets/ASSETS_PROVENANCE_v1_0_0.md; the review cycle in 08-tooling/ch04-deck/REVIEW_v2_0_0.md; earlier versions are in git history." ;
    dcterms:replaces sen0414:Deck_09 ; dcterms:source "03-materials/ch04/rdodi/sen0414_ch04_research_v1_0_0.ttl" .
